    "title": "Yanic makes history in final pick of first round - NewsBreak",
    "text": "BROOKLYN (WTAJ) — Penn State center Yanic Konan Niederhauser made history Wednesday night, becoming the first Nittany Lion drafted in the first round of the NBA Draft by being selected 30th overall by the Los Angeles Clippers. Yanic is the third Penn State alumnus drafted in as many years after Jalen Pickett, and Seth Lundy were selected in the 2023 draft. The Swiss native shot up the draft boards this summer after strong performances at the G League Elite Camp, and NBA combine. He spent one season with the Nittany Lions after beginning his collegiate career at Northern Illinois. This year he averaged 12.9 points-per-game while averaging 6.3 rebounds. Yanic is officially listed at 7-foot and was among 11 internationally born first round selections. The NBA Draft continues with the second round Thursday night. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to DC News Now | DC, Virginia, Maryland News, Weather, Traffic, Sports Live.",
